Z||000000||ponya||01-21-2001||01:51 PM||||I need to change the rear main seal in my <BR>86 SE Automatic. I understand that this seal is a two part seal and that in can be changed in place without removing or seperating transmission from the engine?  Hope I worded that right. 2nd question, would you buy the seal from an Autozone type store or is it better to get that type item from Pontiac? Any advice appreciated.  Thanks   Bob||||reg||5
Z||000001||bHooper||01-21-2001||02:05 PM||||i bought mine from NAPA, and honestly... it looked inferior to the one that was in the car.  my tranny was out at the time, so i changed the seal then.<P>i need to go back and fix it, as there is a weep coming from that area of the shield (getrag).<P><BR>hope this helps some.<P>hoop||||reg||1
Z||000002||2birds||01-21-2001||02:27 PM||||Mine's a one-piece seal (86 GT, Getrag 5-speed, so the transaxle had to be removed.  Changed mine when I did the clutch.  I think the seals were changed between 85 and 88 from a two piece, to a 5 mm one piece, to a 10 mm one piece.  I used a Federal Mogul seal from Discount Auto, no complaints here.  PITA to remove the old one, so I pulled the rear main cap and oil pump and realized it wasn't necessary to do so.  ||||reg||1
